body:
`navigator.clipboard.writeText` is async but isn’t awaited here. If the copy fails (permissions, insecure context, etc.), the UI still shows a success toast. Please `await` the clipboard call and surface an error toast when it rejects (and optionally handle the case where `navigator.clipboard` is unavailable).
```suggestion
        if (!navigator.clipboard) {
          toast.error('Clipboard is unavailable. Copy the password link manually.');
          return;
        }

        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(res.url);
          toast.success('Password link copied! Share it with the user.');
        } catch {
          toast.error('Failed to copy password link');
        }
```

